I think I wanted to live in Berlin  almost as soon as I discovered it what  was below the surface as soon as I  started to to meet the people here who  were engaging in their own projects and  that's kind of the thing that I wanted  to do too and it seemed like a great  place to do it  Oliver Miller was born in 1972 in San  Francisco the youngest of two brothers  seven years later the family moved to  New Mexico  Oliver studied architecture and was  active in the arts eventually he and  other American artists were invited to  participate in an exhibition in Potsdam  just outside Berlin  after finishing his studies in 2000 he  moved to Berlin at first on a temporary  visa and with no real plans then he got  the idea to open a bar it was such a  success that he branched out a few years  later and opened a restaurant  the Nalu diner it's modeled on the  classic diner where breakfast is served  at any time of the day the inspiration  for the restaurant actually came from  going out to clubs and the desire to  have this kind of food late at night  it's a very common thing in America to  have a diner breakfast  in the 24-hour diner at 4:00 or 5:00 in  the morning with bottomless cups of  coffee an American breakfast means first  and foremost lots of combinations  patrons that the Nalu diner can pick can  choose from a variety of options the  menu is centered around eggs for  instance on toast or with hash browns  around 50 combinations are possible  aside from breakfast the diner fries up  classic hamburgers  I loved especially the idea of having  unlimited amount of coffee that you can  get all the time that's that's great and  and plus the hospitality that they the  place the waiters are showing to you and  and the friendliness is really really  great I lived in the USA for a year this  is really quite authentic it's very  close to an American diner food is  fantastic very American two fillings you  get hooked on it and you keep coming  back this markup gun of you know what  mainly sets the American breakfast apart  from the European continental breakfast  are the many cooked components but most  of them can be fixed relatively quickly  and easily Americans call it short-order  cooking pancakes are a breakfast  standard to make them nice and thick the  American Way  the batter has to be right when the  pancakes start getting little bubbles in  the pan they're ready to be flipped  the Naaru diner also serves their own  spiced breakfast sausage patties  a Denver omelet is fried with bell  pepper and chunks of ham and of course  eggs are an essential part of any  American breakfast  all the entrees have served on one  single plate the sweet and the savory  together when one orders breakfast in  American diner the question of how you  want your eggs is is an open one there  is no standard in America you have  scrambled eggs or fried eggs or poached  eggs it's really your choice  the server will always ask how do you  want your eggs and I love hearing this  question because it really means it's  going to be an American breakfast when  you can decide how it is you exactly  want your excellent Oliver Mellor sees  his restaurant as a project that keeps  evolving  the pictures on the walls were made by  himself for artists friends and he keeps  changing them for new ones the  decorations are a hodgepodge of personal  objects and mementos Miller opened his  restaurant in 2012 in Berlin's Eastern  District of prints lat  he lives close by and enjoys the  neighborhoods diversity classes guests  come from all over the world and suits  the Naaru diner the name Nalu diner came  from a conversation with my one of my  old partners who grew up in Hawaii and  actually I've never been know why but  the name is Hawaiian it actually means  surf but not surf in terms of surfing  but surface like a noun it's the top of  the wave as it's breaking and yeah we  just thought okay that's a good name for  for the place at least twice a year  Oliver Miller gets homesick and flies  back to the United States sometimes even  considers moving back entirely someday  maybe  hi we've made a Denver omelet and  buttermilk pancakes and homemade sausage  patty enjoy
 

